Nida patches for goja. scripts/vendorgoja applies this file to upstream
goja, then limits every file to 64-bit platforms.

1. String.prototype.localeCompare compares code points instead of using
   golang.org/x/text/collate. Pele and Temml never call localeCompare, and
   the collation tables add 1.3 MB to the nida binary.

2. Integer conversions that CodeQL flags (go/incorrect-integer-conversion)
   and that are wrong where int is 32 bits:
   - Number.prototype.toString and BigInt.prototype.toString check the
     radix before converting it to int, so 2**32 + 10 is a RangeError, not
     radix 10.
   - Array.prototype.join counts in int64.
   - String.prototype.split caps its limit at MaxInt32 before converting.
   - Shrinking an array compares indexes as int64.
   - Array lengths are read with toUint32 instead of uint32(ToInteger()).

